Purpose: Resolve the new tab page through corvid::NtpOverride so extension overrides load without flash and fall back to corvid://newtab.
Area: extensions
Files: chrome/browser/extensions/extension_url_overrides.cc (HandleChromeURLOverride at line 455, reverse variant near 473); chrome/browser/ui/webui/chrome_web_ui_controller_factory.cc (call sites at 284 and 473)
Rebase risk: medium
Origin: original (written for Corvid; no third-party patch text reused)
Status: SPEC (exact edits from the VM builder's read-only greps on 155.0.8059.39, relayed 2026-10-13). Still NO diff hunks and the edits are not applied or built. Generate the diff on the tree with scripts/refresh-patches.sh.

Change (exact edits; extension_web_ui.cc no longer exists upstream, the old file list is obsolete):
1. extensions::ExtensionUrlOverrides::HandleChromeURLOverride(GURL*, BrowserContext*) (extension_url_overrides.cc:455) returns the first override from GetOverridesForChromeURL. For the newtab host only, replace "first override" by corvid::ResolveNewTab(candidates, picked, incognito, force_default) from src-overlay/corvid/extensions/ntp_override.h: build NtpCandidate{extension_id, enabled_at, overrides_newtab, incognito_allowed} from the overriding extensions, take picked from the Corvid pref, and rewrite the URL to the chosen extension's page or leave it for corvid://newtab when the result is empty.
2. chrome_web_ui_controller_factory.cc:284 (forward) and :473 (reverse variant): confirm no change is needed once step 1 is in place; the reverse path must keep mapping the extension URL back to chrome://newtab for display.
3. chrome/browser/search/search.cc (second grep round, +/-2 lines): GetNewTabPageURL (:337-339) returns NewTabURLDetails::ForProfile(profile).url. ForProfile is at :166; the off-the-record check is at :170. Desktop local_url is set at :188-194 (chrome://newtab when the default engine is Google, else kChromeUINewTabPageThirdPartyURL); for a non-Google default it starts from the provider's new_tab_url_ref (:206-209) and returns it at :225 if valid and secure, else local_url (:203/:212/:215). Edit: at the top of ForProfile, before the :170 check, return the Corvid new tab URL (corvid://newtab, which ui/0200 maps to chrome://corvid-newtab) so every case, incognito included, lands on the Corvid NTP; extension overrides are then applied by step 1. UNTESTED: confirm that returning this early does not break the incognito NTP, and that HandleChromeURLOverride still sees chrome://newtab for the override to apply (if the early return bypasses it, return chrome://newtab here and let step 1 plus ui/0200 do the mapping).
4. Related files to read when writing the hunk, not edit unless a grep says so: extension_url_overrides_registrar.cc, installed_loader.cc, extension_util.cc, startup_tab_provider.cc.

